Recreating paragraphs for each size will do a lot of unnecessary work, instead font of the spans should be updated. `RichTextLabel` have `_update_line_font` method for this purpose and can be used as example.

Something like:
```c++
RID t = p_paragraph->get_rid();
int spans = TS->shaped_get_span_count(t);
for (int i = 0; i < spans; i++) {
	TS->shaped_set_span_update_font(t, i, font->get_rids(), font_size, font->get_opentype_features());
}
```

